-- title:
--   Supersingular chart and q+1 nodes over the level-q field
-- statement:
--   Throughout, $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ is an algebraic closure of $\mathbb Q$, Laurent series are Hahn series over $\mathbb Z$ in the $q$-expansion variable, and $j$ denotes the Laurent series `jq` $=t^{-1}\cdot$`jNumQ`, the expansion of the modular $j$-invariant, which lies in the full level-$M'$ field `modularFunctionFieldFull M'` $=\mathbb Q(\{\,$`qExpand ℚ d jq` $: d\mid M'\,\})$.
--
--   **Data and hypotheses.** *(Level.)* A prime $q$ with $5\le q$, and a nonzero natural number $M'$ with $q\nmid M'$.
--
--   *(Valuation ring over $q$.)* A valuation subring $A\subseteq\overline{\mathbb Q}$ with `hA : A.LiesOverPrime q`, i.e. $q$ is a non-unit of $A$; write $\kappa=$ `ResidueField A`.
--
--   *(Supersingular places.)* A finite set $W$ of places of `modularFunctionFieldC κ M'` $=\kappa(\,$`jqModC κ`$,\,$`jqNModC κ M'`$\,)$ over $\kappa$ — a place being a valuation subring containing the constants, different from the whole field, with principal ideals — together with `hW`, which says that $W$ consists exactly of the members of `ssPlaces q M' κ`: those $w$ which are rational (the map $\kappa\to$ residue field of $w$ is surjective), satisfy the predicate `IsAffineGeomPlace κ M' w`, and whose value `w.evalAt (jGeomGen κ M')` lies in `ssJSet q κ`. A distinguished element $s\in W$ is fixed.
--
--   *(Comparison of function fields.)* `hle` asserts `modularFunctionFieldBar M' ≤ fieldBar q M'`, where the left-hand side is the intermediate field of the Laurent series over $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ generated by the coefficientwise image of `modularFunctionFieldFull M'`, and `fieldBar q M'` $=$ `xHFunctionFieldBar (q^2*M') (levelH q M')` is the corresponding field for the group $H=\ker\big((\mathbb Z/q^2M')^\times\to(\mathbb Z/q)^\times\big)$, the units congruent to $1$ modulo $q$.
--
--   *(Reduction datum.)* $R_0$, a `ConstantReduction A (modularFunctionFieldBar M') (modularFunctionFieldC κ M')`: a valuation subring `R₀.integers` of `modularFunctionFieldBar M'` meeting the constants exactly in $A$, a surjective ring homomorphism `R₀.residue` onto `modularFunctionFieldC κ M'` with kernel the maximal ideal and inducing on constants the residue map of $A$, a map on places preserving degrees and compatible with push-forward of divisors of functions with nonzero residue, and the property that every nonzero function becomes a function with nonzero residue after multiplication by a constant. The hypothesis `hR₀` requires that for every Laurent series $y$ over $A$ whose coefficientwise image in $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ lies in `modularFunctionFieldBar M'`, that element lies in `R₀.integers` and its residue, read as a Laurent series over $\kappa$, is the coefficientwise reduction of $y$.
--
--   *(Small field.)* An intermediate field $k_0$ of $\overline{\mathbb Q}/\mathbb Q$ and $\pi_0\in k_0$ with $\pi_0\in A$, such that $A\cap k_0$ (the comap of $A$ along $k_0\hookrightarrow\overline{\mathbb Q}$) is a discrete valuation ring (`hdvr`) with maximal ideal generated by $\pi_0$ (`hunif`), is henselian local (`hhens`), has algebraically closed residue field (`hres`), and such that every $a\in A$ is congruent modulo the maximal ideal of $A$ to some $c\in k_0\cap A$ (`hκ`).
--
--   *(Auxiliary prime and roots of unity.)* A prime $\ell$ with $3\le\ell$, $\ell\neq q$, $\ell\nmid M'$; an element $\zeta_0\in k_0$ which is a primitive $q\ell$-th root of unity in $\overline{\mathbb Q}$; an element $\varpi_t\in k_0$ with $\varpi_t\in A$ and $\varpi_t^{\,q^2-1}=q\,u$ for some unit $u$ of $A$.
--
--   *(Base layer.)* An intermediate field $K_b$ of $\overline{\mathbb Q}/k_0$ with $K_b=\bot$ (so $K_b=k_0$), a valuation subring $A_b\subseteq K_b$ whose members are exactly the elements of $K_b$ lying in $A$, and a nonzero $\varpi_b\in A_b$ generating the maximal ideal of $A_b$.
--
--   **Conclusion.** Give `fieldBar q M'` the $k_0$-algebra structure obtained by composing $k_0\hookrightarrow\overline{\mathbb Q}$ with $\overline{\mathbb Q}\to$ `fieldBar q M'`. Let $F_0$ be any intermediate field of `fieldBar q M'` over $k_0$ which is characterised by the stated condition: an element $f$ of `fieldBar q M'` lies in $F_0$ if and only if every Laurent coefficient of $f$ lies in (the image of) $k_0$. Then there is a valuation subring $W_0$ of $F_0$ with the following properties.
--
--   (1) For $x\in k_0$: $x\in A$ if and only if the image of $x$ in $F_0$ lies in $W_0$.
--
--   (2) $W_0$ is a discrete valuation ring.
--
--   (3) The image of $\pi_0$ lies in $W_0$ and generates the maximal ideal of $W_0$.
--
--   (4) *(Centre at $s$.)* For every Laurent series $g$ over $\mathbb Q$ lying in `modularFunctionFieldFull M'` whose coefficientwise image lies in `R₀.integers`, such that $g$ is regular wherever $j$ is (for every place $P$ of `modularFunctionFieldBar M'` over $\overline{\mathbb Q}$, $0\le P.\mathrm{ord}(j)$ implies $0\le P.\mathrm{ord}(g)$), and whose $R_0$-residue lies in the valuation subring of $s$: the image of $g$ in `fieldBar q M'` lies in $F_0$ and in $W_0$, and for every $c\in k_0$ with $c\in A$ whose residue in $\kappa$ equals $s.\mathrm{evalAt}$ of the $R_0$-residue of $g$, the difference $g-c$ lies in the maximal ideal of $W_0$.
--
--   (5) *(Level stability.)* For every $\zeta\in$ `Idx q` (a primitive $q$-th root of unity in $\overline{\mathbb Q}$), every $\gamma\in SL_2(\mathbb Z)$ with $\gamma\in\Gamma_0(M')$ and every $f\in F_0$ with `levelAutBar q M' ζ γ f` $\in F_0$: $f\in W_0$ if and only if `levelAutBar q M' ζ γ f` $\in W_0$. Here `levelAutBar q M' ζ γ` is the $\overline{\mathbb Q}$-automorphism of `fieldBar q M'` satisfying `IsLevelAutBar q M' ζ γ` — the action of $\gamma$ conjugated by `conjElem q γ` on quotients of $q$-expansions of modular forms for $\Gamma_H(q^2M')$, measured through embeddings $\overline{\mathbb Q}\to\mathbb C$ sending $\zeta$ to $e^{2\pi i/q}$ — if such an automorphism exists, and the identity otherwise.
--
--   (6) *(Affine chart over $A_b$.)* There are a subring $B$ of `fieldBar q M'` and an $A_b$-algebra structure on $B$ such that:
--
--   (6a) the structure map sends $a\in A_b$ to the image of $a$ under $K_b\subseteq\overline{\mathbb Q}\to$ `fieldBar q M'`;
--
--   (6b) $B$ is contained in the compositum of `IntermediateField.adjoin k₀` (image of $K_b$) and $F_0$;
--
--   (6c) every element of that compositum is of the form $g/h$ with $g,h\in B$, $h\neq0$;
--
--   (6d) $B$ is formally smooth and of finite presentation over $A_b$;
--
--   (6e) $B/\varpi_b B$ has Krull dimension at most $1$;
--
--   (6f) every element of $B$ lies in $F_0$ and in $W_0$;
--
--   (6g) the image of $\varpi_b$ in $B$ is a prime element;
--
--   (6h) an element $f\in F_0$ lies in $W_0$ if and only if $f\,h=g$ for some $g,h\in B$ with $\varpi_b\nmid h$ in $B$;
--
--   (6i) the image of $j$ in `fieldBar q M'` lies in $B$;
--
--   (6j) $B$ is stable under `levelAutBar q M' ζ γ` for every $\zeta\in$ `Idx q` and every $\gamma\in\Gamma_0(M')$;
--
--   (6k) there is $b\in B$ with $b\in F_0$ such that $b\notin V$ for every valuation subring $V$ of $F_0$ satisfying: $V$ meets $k_0$ exactly in $A$, $\pi_0$ lies in the maximal ideal of $V$, $j$ lies in $V$, and for every monic polynomial $p$ over $k_0$ with all coefficients in $A$, if $p(j)\in V$ then $p(j)$ is a unit at $V$;
--
--   (6l) for every $s'\in W$ with $s'\neq s$ there is $b\in B$ with $b\in F_0$ such that $b\notin V$ for every valuation subring $V$ of $F_0$ which meets $k_0$ exactly in $A$ and satisfies the condition of (4) with $s'$ in place of $s$ and $V$ in place of $W_0$;
--
--   (6m) *(Drinfeld description of the special fibre.)* for every $\mathbb F_{q^2}$-algebra structure on $\kappa$, every witness that [`DrinfeldCurve.CoordRing q κ`](def/DrinfeldCurve_CoordRing.html#L21) $=\kappa[x_0,x_1]/(\mathrm{drinfeldPoly}-1)$ is a domain, and every $\zeta\in$ `Idx q`, there are a subgroup $C_s$ of the $(q+1)$-st roots of unity of $\mathbb F_{q^2}$ and a ring homomorphism $\rho:B\to$ [`DrinfeldCurve.quotField q κ Cs`](def/ModularCurve_FullLevelSemistableCoveringW2.html#L32) (the subfield of the Drinfeld function field fixed by the `hFunctionFieldAction` of the elements $(1,\zeta')$, $\zeta'\in C_s$) with: $\#C_s=2\cdot$ `placeWidthChar q M' s`, which for $q\ge5$ is $\mathrm{jWidth}$ of $s.\mathrm{evalAt}($`jGeomGen κ M'`$)$ divided by `placeRamificationJ M' s` $=\mathrm{ord}_s($`jGeomGen` $-\,s.\mathrm{evalAt}($`jGeomGen`$))$; $\ker\rho=(\varpi_b)$; $\rho$ sends the image of $a\in A_b$ to the image in `quotField` of the residue of $a$ in $\kappa$; every element of `quotField` is of the form $\rho(g)/\rho(h)$ with $g,h\in B$, $\rho(h)\neq0$; the image of $\rho$ consists exactly of those $z$ whose image in the Drinfeld function field lies in the image of `CoordRing q κ`; and $\rho$ is equivariant, in the sense that for $\gamma\in\Gamma_0(M')$ with $(\,$`redQ q γ`$,1)\in$ `hSubgroup q` and $f\in B$ with `levelAutBar q M' ζ γ⁻¹ f` $\in B$, the image of $\rho($`levelAutBar q M' ζ γ⁻¹ f`$)$ in the Drinfeld function field is `hFunctionFieldAction q κ` of $(\,$`redQ q γ`$,1)$ applied to the image of $\rho(f)$;
--
--   (6n) *(Nodes.)* the image of $j$ lies in `R₀.integers`, its $R_0$-residue lies in the valuation subring of $s$, [`ModularCurve.jqNModC (AlgebraicClosure ℚ) q`](def/ModularCurve_JqCoeff.html#L18) (the expansion of $j(q\tau)$) lies in `fieldBar q M'`, there is $a_0\in k_0$ with $a_0\in A$ whose residue satisfies $\overline{a_0}^{\,q}=s.\mathrm{evalAt}$ of the $R_0$-residue of $j$, and there is a finite set `nodes` of subrings of $F_0$ such that:
--
--   • `nodes.card` $=q+1$;
--
--   • *(common chart)* there is a subring $B_c$ of $F_0$ of the form `Subring.closure` of the set of images of elements of $k_0\cap A$ together with a finite set $T$, such that every $O\in$ `nodes` contains $B_c$ and is its localisation: $f\in O$ if and only if $f\,h=g$ for some $g,h\in B_c$ with $h$ a unit of $O$ whenever $h\in O$;
--
--   • *(level action on nodes)* for every $\zeta$ and every $\gamma\in\Gamma_0(M')$ and every $O\in$ `nodes` there is $O'\in$ `nodes` with $f\in O\iff$ `levelAutBar q M' ζ γ f` $\in O'$ for all $f\in F_0$ with `levelAutBar q M' ζ γ f` $\in F_0$;
--
--   • *(transitivity)* for every $\zeta$ and all $O,O'\in$ `nodes` there is $\gamma\in\Gamma_0(M')$ realising this correspondence from $O$ to $O'$;
--
--   • *(pairwise distinctness)* for $O\neq O'$ in `nodes` there is $f\in O\cap O'$ which is a non-unit of $O$ and a unit of $O'$;
--
--   • *(the nodes dominate the fibre over $s$)* for every valuation subring $V$ of $F_0$ which meets $k_0$ exactly in $A$ and satisfies the condition of (4) with $V$ in place of $W_0$: either every element of $B$ lies in $F_0$ and in $V$, or there is $O\in$ `nodes` with $O\subseteq V$ and such that every non-unit of $O$ lies in the maximal ideal of $V$;
--
--   • and for every $O\in$ `nodes`: $O\subseteq W_0$; $O$ is local and noetherian; $O$ meets $k_0$ exactly in $A$ (for $x\in k_0$: $x\in A\iff$ the image of $x$ lies in $O$); every $f\in O$ differs from the image of some $x\in k_0\cap A$ by a non-unit of $O$; and there are an integer $E_0\ge1$, a unit $v$ of $k_0\cap A$ (i.e. $v,v^{-1}\in A$) with $\pi_0^{E_0}=\varpi_t^{\,2\,w}\,v$ where $w=$ `placeWidthChar q M' s`, a witness that $\pi_0$ lies in $O$, elements $c_x,c_y\in O$, a unit $u$ of $O$, a ring isomorphism $\iota$ from the adic completion of $O$ at its maximal ideal onto the crossing model `UVCrossingModel` of the adic completion $\widehat{A\cap k_0}$ at the parameter $\pi_0^{E_0}$, that is $\widehat{A\cap k_0}[[U,V]]/(UV-\pi_0^{E_0})$, and units $\gamma_U,\gamma_V$ of that model, such that:
--
--   – $c_x c_y=\pi_0^{E_0}u$ in $O$;
--
--   – $\iota$ carries the image of each $x\in k_0\cap A$ to the constant $x$ of the model;
--
--   – $\iota(c_x)=\gamma_U\cdot U$ and $\iota(c_y)=\gamma_V\cdot V$;
--
--   – $c_y$ lies in $W_0$ and in its maximal ideal, while $c_x$, whenever it lies in $W_0$, is a unit there;
--
--   – *(Hasse export on the moduli $j$)* the element `jqNModC (AlgebraicClosure ℚ) q` $-\,a_0$ lies in $F_0$ and in $O$, and there are $e\ge1$ and a unit $w_V$ of the model with $\iota$ of this element equal to $w_V\cdot V^{e}$;
--
--   – *(the Igusa valuation at the node)* there is a valuation subring $W_x$ of $F_0$ with: $O\subseteq W_x$; $W_x$ meets $k_0$ exactly in $A$; $W_x$ is a discrete valuation ring; the image of $\pi_0$ generates the maximal ideal of $W_x$; there is $t\in W_x$ such that for every polynomial $p$ over $k_0$ with all coefficients in $A$, if $p(t)$ lies in the maximal ideal of $W_x$ then so does every coefficient of $p$; $c_x$ lies in the maximal ideal of $W_x$ and $c_y$ is a unit there; for every $g$ as in (4) (in `modularFunctionFieldFull M'`, with image in `R₀.integers`, regular wherever $j$ is) the image of $g$ lies in $F_0$ and in $W_x$, it lies in the maximal ideal of $W_x$ if and only if its $R_0$-residue is $0$, and if that residue lies in the valuation subring of $s$ then the image of $g$ lies in $O$ and, for every $c\in k_0\cap A$ whose residue equals $s.\mathrm{evalAt}$ of the residue of $g$, the difference of $g$ and $c$ is a non-unit of $O$; and, finally, for every $O'\in$ `nodes` with $O'\neq O$ there is $f\in O'$ with $f\notin W_x$;
--
--   – *(affine chart at the node)* there is a subring $B_x$ of $F_0$ with: every $f\in B_x$ lies in $B$ and in $O$; every $f\in B_x$ is regular wherever $j$ is (for every place $P$ of `fieldBar q M'` over $\overline{\mathbb Q}$, $0\le P.\mathrm{ord}(j)$ implies $0\le P.\mathrm{ord}(f)$); $O$ is the localisation of $B_x$ in the sense that $f\in O$ if and only if $f\,h=g$ with $g,h\in B_x$ and $h$ a unit of $O$ whenever $h\in O$; every $f\in F_0$ is of the form $g/h$ with $g,h\in B_x$, $h\neq0$; $B_x$ is the `Subring.closure` of the images of the elements of $k_0\cap A$ together with a finite set $T$; and there is $b\in B_x$ such that, for every valuation subring $V$ of $F_0$ which meets $k_0$ exactly in $A$, has $\pi_0$ in its maximal ideal, contains $j$, and is such that $p(j)$ is a unit at $V$ for every monic polynomial $p$ over $k_0$ with coefficients in $A$ for which $p(j)\in V$, the existence of some $f\in O$ with $f\notin V$ forces $b\notin V$.
--
--   This is the packaged semistable-model statement at a supersingular place $s$ of the level-$M'$ modular curve, transported to the level-$q$ field `fieldBar q M'`: a discrete valuation ring $W_0$ centred at $s$, a formally smooth finitely presented chart $B$ over the base layer $A_b$ whose special fibre is identified with a quotient of the Drinfeld curve of level $q$, and a set of $q+1$ nodes on the fibre, each with a crossing model $UV=\pi_0^{E_0}$, the Hasse-type relation for $j(q\tau)$, and an Igusa valuation separating it from the other nodes. It is the form of the statement used by [`ModularCurve.FullLevel.exists_supersingularDVR_affineChart_poles_moduliHasse_commonChart_nodes_of_levelField`](thm.html#ModularCurve.FullLevel.exists_supersingularDVR_affineChart_poles_moduliHasse_commonChart_nodes_of_levelField), and it is obtained from the variant that in addition records the tame-inertia clause.
